1
00:00:00,043 --> 00:00:01,503
(All child actor scenes were filmed with a guardian present...)

2
00:00:01,573 --> 00:00:03,043
(with professional staff and in accordance with safety guidelines.)

3
00:00:38,013 --> 00:00:39,013
Won Ho.

4
00:00:41,313 --> 00:00:42,353
Wait a minute.

5
00:00:58,533 --> 00:00:59,533
Let's...

6
00:01:01,503 --> 00:01:03,003
Let's get divorced.

7
00:01:29,433 --> 00:01:31,163
(Episode 1)

8
00:01:56,753 --> 00:02:00,463
Hello, my followers. Good morning.

9
00:02:02,633 --> 00:02:04,563
Looks like more people are joining.

10
00:02:05,233 --> 00:02:06,633
Shall we begin? Yes.

11
00:02:07,333 --> 00:02:09,133
Hello, my followers.

12
00:02:11,373 --> 00:02:13,243
Do you know what today is?

13
00:02:13,643 --> 00:02:16,413
Today is the special day we at J&White...

14
00:02:16,973 --> 00:02:19,583
are so excited to present our free dress-fitting event.

15
00:02:22,813 --> 00:02:24,983
For all you brides-to-be out there,

16
00:02:25,053 --> 00:02:26,623
when you're out dress shopping,

17
00:02:26,683 --> 00:02:28,823
the fees for trying on each dress...

18
00:02:29,823 --> 00:02:31,253
can be a real burden, can't they?

19
00:02:31,723 --> 00:02:33,823
If you visit us at J&White today,

20
00:02:33,993 --> 00:02:36,463
you can try on as many dresses as you like,

21
00:02:36,533 --> 00:02:38,333
not for half off, but for free.

22
00:02:38,393 --> 00:02:39,533
(I want to see your husband.)

23
00:02:39,603 --> 00:02:41,103
My husband?

24
00:02:41,163 --> 00:02:42,803
(An opportunity like this doesn't come often.)

25
00:02:42,873 --> 00:02:44,003
It sure doesn't.

26
00:02:44,333 --> 00:02:46,673
So be sure to come and see my husband in person.

27
00:02:47,743 --> 00:02:50,573
But this is a little secret just between us.

28
00:02:51,043 --> 00:02:54,643
My husband's heart is even more handsome than his face.

29
00:02:55,513 --> 00:02:56,953
Even today, just for me,

30
00:02:57,213 --> 00:03:00,283
he made me fresh juice before he went to work.

31
00:03:00,423 --> 00:03:01,583
(You're so pretty. Will Designer Ji be there?)

32
00:03:01,653 --> 00:03:02,753
(Will we get to see him in person?)

33
00:03:03,823 --> 00:03:05,863
Anyway, my dear followers,

34
00:03:06,223 --> 00:03:09,763
I put so much effort into preparing today's event,

35
00:03:09,963 --> 00:03:12,903
so don't miss this opportunity. Please visit our store today.

36
00:03:13,203 --> 00:03:17,633
It starts at 11:00 a.m. Okay, see you all later. Bye.

37
00:03:17,703 --> 00:03:19,403
(See you at the store. I've been waiting for this day.)

38
00:03:19,473 --> 00:03:20,543
(Livestream ended)

39
00:03:39,023 --> 00:03:41,223
The forecast for today is mostly clear skies nationwide,

40
00:03:41,293 --> 00:03:43,233
with some occasional clouds.

41
00:03:43,333 --> 00:03:46,903
Thick fog has formed in the inland regions this morning,

42
00:03:47,033 --> 00:03:50,673
so please be cautious during your morning commute.

43
00:03:50,973 --> 00:03:52,773
Strong winds are expected in mountains...

44
00:03:52,843 --> 00:03:54,403
and along the east coast in Gangwon Province.

45
00:04:40,053 --> 00:04:41,083
Good morning.

46
00:04:41,523 --> 00:04:42,593
Not for me.

47
00:04:43,123 --> 00:04:45,723
I am in a terrible mood right now.

48
00:04:46,663 --> 00:04:48,663
Is something wrong?

49
00:04:48,893 --> 00:04:50,093
Do you really need to ask?

50
00:04:50,493 --> 00:04:52,733
Take a good, hard look at yourself.

51
00:04:53,303 --> 00:04:56,303
Manager Song, did I do something wrong?

52
00:04:56,433 --> 00:04:59,203
You went drinking again last night, didn't you?

53
00:04:59,573 --> 00:05:01,473
Yes, I did.

54
00:05:01,643 --> 00:05:04,673
Don't you have any self-control?

55
00:05:04,913 --> 00:05:07,613
I try, but it's not that easy...

56
00:05:07,683 --> 00:05:11,613
Then why do you keep breaking your promise, you idiot?

57
00:05:16,853 --> 00:05:20,163
You're not an ex-husband, you're my nemesis.

58
00:05:27,703 --> 00:05:28,733
Vice President Kang.

59
00:05:29,703 --> 00:05:30,903
Good morning.

60
00:05:31,533 --> 00:05:33,373
- Yes. - Good morning.

61
00:05:37,343 --> 00:05:39,483
Company sales have been dropping lately,

62
00:05:39,783 --> 00:05:41,543
so let's make today's event a success...

63
00:05:41,913 --> 00:05:43,683
and really turn things around.

64
00:05:45,113 --> 00:05:46,123
- Yes. - Yes.

65
00:05:46,453 --> 00:05:48,023
You two, prepare the pamphlets...

66
00:05:48,083 --> 00:05:50,053
and dress lists so you can immediately...

67
00:05:50,123 --> 00:05:52,093
answer any questions customers have when they arrive.

68
00:05:52,293 --> 00:05:55,023
We'll get a lot of customers this time, right?

69
00:05:55,323 --> 00:05:58,533
Of course. CEO Baek worked so hard on this event.

70
00:05:58,803 --> 00:06:01,633
This event will be a success, and company sales will soar.

71
00:06:02,003 --> 00:06:03,003
Let's do this.

72
00:06:03,873 --> 00:06:06,703
Oh, and please finish the showroom display this morning.

73
00:06:06,803 --> 00:06:09,343
I already finished that.

74
00:06:09,913 --> 00:06:11,813
I just checked, and there was nothing there.

75
00:06:11,973 --> 00:06:14,283
What? That can't be right.

76
00:06:16,253 --> 00:06:19,023
Hey. What do you think you're doing?

77
00:06:19,523 --> 00:06:20,883
Where are the dresses that were here?

78
00:06:21,153 --> 00:06:25,053
CEO Ji called and told me to replace them with these.

79
00:06:26,893 --> 00:06:28,263
CEO Ji?

80
00:06:30,033 --> 00:06:31,093
It's fine.

81
00:06:32,263 --> 00:06:34,003
Just do what CEO Ji wants.

82
00:06:34,903 --> 00:06:36,673
- Okay. - Really?

83
00:06:37,703 --> 00:06:40,943
But you worked on that display day and night.

84
00:06:42,173 --> 00:06:46,113
Well, we have to respect the opinion...

85
00:06:46,813 --> 00:06:47,843
of a J&White designer.

86
00:06:49,453 --> 00:06:50,753
Excuse me? Is anyone here?

87
00:06:51,383 --> 00:06:52,483
Yes. Welcome.

88
00:06:52,883 --> 00:06:56,223
- I'm here for a dress quote. - Of course.

89
00:06:56,623 --> 00:06:57,623
No, I'll take care of it.

90
00:06:58,393 --> 00:06:59,593
I can help you.

91
00:07:01,163 --> 00:07:03,863
Yes, please fill this out.

92
00:07:03,863 --> 00:07:05,563
CEO Baek is really...

93
00:07:06,133 --> 00:07:08,163
She's such a class act.

94
00:07:11,833 --> 00:07:12,943
I'm Baek Mi Young.

95
00:07:13,403 --> 00:07:16,213
The CEO of the all-in-one wedding company, J&White.

96
00:07:17,643 --> 00:07:21,643
For my company, there's nothing I won't do or can't accomplish.

97
00:07:21,713 --> 00:07:24,583
I think any of these would look good on you.

98
00:07:24,583 --> 00:07:25,583
Then please choose one...

99
00:07:25,583 --> 00:07:26,683
Yes, ma'am.

100
00:07:26,823 --> 00:07:28,853
Yes, the preliminary fitting is done.

101
00:07:28,953 --> 00:07:31,893
Yes, you just need to come in for one more fitting.

102
00:07:32,053 --> 00:07:33,763
You're not available?

103
00:07:34,393 --> 00:07:37,933
In that case, I can bring the dress to you.

104
00:07:37,933 --> 00:07:38,933
Yes, of course.

105
00:07:39,163 --> 00:07:40,833
If a path is blocked, I forge a new one.

106
00:07:43,233 --> 00:07:46,843
If there's something I don't know, I learn it to get the job done.

107
00:07:48,643 --> 00:07:52,783
But even I had a mountain I couldn't easily climb.

108
00:07:54,043 --> 00:07:57,483
The famous designer, Ji Won Ho.

109
00:07:59,623 --> 00:08:00,923
My husband.

110
00:08:01,923 --> 00:08:05,393
(Special Event: Free Fitting Event for Brides- And Grooms-To-Be)

111
00:08:06,063 --> 00:08:08,063
(Free Fitting for Brides-To-Be)

112
00:08:14,333 --> 00:08:16,333
This one needs to have the same beads.

113
00:08:24,213 --> 00:08:25,343
I can't stand the sight of him.

114
00:08:32,553 --> 00:08:34,183
I can't believe people throw trash on the floor...

115
00:08:34,253 --> 00:08:38,223
when the can is right there. I'm so sick of it. Seriously.

116
00:08:43,033 --> 00:08:45,663
- What do you think you're doing? - You'll clean it up anyway.

117
00:08:47,563 --> 00:08:48,633
(Jihwaja Motel)

118
00:08:48,703 --> 00:08:49,703
Excuse me.

119
00:08:49,973 --> 00:08:52,703
Come on, you can't just throw that at someone.

120
00:08:53,503 --> 00:08:54,503
So what?

121
00:08:55,543 --> 00:08:56,543
Let go.

122
00:08:59,183 --> 00:09:00,513
Disgusting.

123
00:09:00,813 --> 00:09:02,513
You're just a motel cleaner.

124
00:09:08,753 --> 00:09:10,193
(Jihwaja Motel)

125
00:09:10,293 --> 00:09:11,323
That son of a...

126
00:09:38,913 --> 00:09:40,253
Hey, you punk.

127
00:09:42,523 --> 00:09:43,523
What?

128
00:10:00,173 --> 00:10:01,173
(Jihwaja Motel)

129
00:10:01,173 --> 00:10:03,813
I told you to control that temper.

130
00:10:04,243 --> 00:10:07,213
What were you thinking, throwing something at a guest?

131
00:10:07,613 --> 00:10:09,613
You're lucky I was able to calm him down with an apology.

132
00:10:09,983 --> 00:10:11,653
Mom, you're going to get arrested doing that.

133
00:10:11,713 --> 00:10:13,553
My son was being humiliated.

134
00:10:13,623 --> 00:10:15,953
What parent would just stand by and watch that?

135
00:10:16,253 --> 00:10:17,723
Still, you can't just do that to a guest.

136
00:10:17,793 --> 00:10:20,693
Guest or not, family always comes first.

137
00:10:21,793 --> 00:10:22,893
Right, Ha Neul?

138
00:10:23,033 --> 00:10:24,563
Yes, Grandma is the best.

139
00:10:24,733 --> 00:10:27,363
Oh, you're such a sweet little thing.

140
00:10:29,703 --> 00:10:30,703
Anyway,

141
00:10:30,773 --> 00:10:33,943
you know what this weekend is, right?

142
00:10:34,303 --> 00:10:36,243
It's the weekend, so it's when the soap opera is on.

143
00:10:36,413 --> 00:10:39,083
Hey, you punk. You don't even know your own mother's birthday?

144
00:10:40,713 --> 00:10:42,183
Everything about you is bad,

145
00:10:42,243 --> 00:10:44,213
but your memory is the worst. Got it?

146
00:10:45,683 --> 00:10:49,293
Speaking of which, you know my friend Gi Sun, right?

147
00:10:51,253 --> 00:10:52,763
Her daughter-in-law, you know,

148
00:10:52,993 --> 00:10:55,093
apparently prepared a birthday feast for her...

149
00:10:55,163 --> 00:10:56,293
that was fit for a king.

150
00:10:56,633 --> 00:10:59,303
Some women have all the luck.

151
00:10:59,463 --> 00:11:00,763
What daughter-in-law cooks a birthday meal...

152
00:11:00,833 --> 00:11:01,833
for her mother-in-law these days?

153
00:11:01,903 --> 00:11:03,303
I'm serious.

154
00:11:03,833 --> 00:11:06,443
Mom, don't even think about it.

155
00:11:06,703 --> 00:11:08,673
Maybe some spending money or a trip, but a birthday meal?

156
00:11:09,113 --> 00:11:10,973
My mom sure has big dreams.

157
00:11:11,113 --> 00:11:14,213
What? Big dreams? You brat!

158
00:11:14,283 --> 00:11:16,513
- Ha Neul, it's time for preschool. - Okay.

159
00:11:16,583 --> 00:11:17,583
Say goodbye to Grandma.

160
00:11:17,853 --> 00:11:20,583
- Goodbye. - Bye, Ha Neul.

161
00:11:25,623 --> 00:11:27,423
(Happy Birthday)

162
00:11:28,423 --> 00:11:29,433
Right.

163
00:11:30,133 --> 00:11:33,503
I'm going to have my daughter-in-law make me a birthday meal.

164
00:11:53,723 --> 00:11:54,983
It hurts to look.

165
00:11:56,723 --> 00:11:57,893
How can there not even be...

166
00:12:01,763 --> 00:12:02,963
one person here?

167
00:12:03,433 --> 00:12:05,293
It's the recession, I suppose.

168
00:12:07,333 --> 00:12:09,503
Are we going to go out of business at this rate?

169
00:12:09,973 --> 00:12:11,033
Out of business?

170
00:12:11,833 --> 00:12:12,843
Director Song.

171
00:12:13,043 --> 00:12:14,203
You take that back right now.

172
00:12:14,473 --> 00:12:16,773
- Take it back. - I take it back.

173
00:12:19,443 --> 00:12:20,543
I guess...

174
00:12:21,843 --> 00:12:23,683
the event wasn't promoted as well as we'd hoped.

175
00:12:23,983 --> 00:12:25,953
It wasn't just "not promoted", it was completely wrong.

176
00:12:27,353 --> 00:12:28,753
The focus was all wrong.

177
00:12:29,493 --> 00:12:31,023
Instead of doing some pointless free event,

178
00:12:31,093 --> 00:12:33,563
we should've been promoting the kinds of dresses we actually sell.

179
00:12:34,763 --> 00:12:36,693
Show that J&White is different from other shops.

180
00:12:36,763 --> 00:12:39,463
That we have something special.

181
00:12:39,763 --> 00:12:42,333
That's why I told you from the start this was a bad idea.

182
00:12:47,073 --> 00:12:48,073
I was right, wasn't I?

183
00:12:54,743 --> 00:12:56,053
(Free Fitting for Brides-To-Be)

184
00:12:57,953 --> 00:12:59,053
Welcome.

185
00:13:00,023 --> 00:13:01,023
Hello.

186
00:13:01,083 --> 00:13:03,623
Are you here for our event?

187
00:13:03,953 --> 00:13:05,023
Actually, no.

188
00:13:05,253 --> 00:13:07,593
I'm here to see the CEOs.

189
00:13:08,863 --> 00:13:10,293
The CEOs?

190
00:13:12,963 --> 00:13:14,103
(Dream Project: Wedding Edition)

191
00:13:14,163 --> 00:13:15,333
(Kim Hye Won, Writer, CSB)

192
00:13:15,403 --> 00:13:17,903
You want to cast us in a variety show?

193
00:13:18,303 --> 00:13:21,703
Yes. Have you ever heard of a show called "Dream Project"?

194
00:13:26,343 --> 00:13:27,443
Oh, I know that show.

195
00:13:27,813 --> 00:13:31,053
It's the one with all the famous experts...

196
00:13:31,113 --> 00:13:32,983
who grant wishes for regular people.

197
00:13:33,553 --> 00:13:35,123
- That one? - Yes.

198
00:13:35,123 --> 00:13:38,053
- Didn't they build a house once? - Oh, yes.

199
00:13:38,423 --> 00:13:39,563
Yes, that's the one.

200
00:13:39,793 --> 00:13:42,733
So this time around, we're planning a wedding theme.

201
00:13:42,963 --> 00:13:45,563
For people who couldn't have a wedding due to their circumstances,

202
00:13:45,833 --> 00:13:47,533
we'll be making them their wedding dresses.

203
00:13:49,803 --> 00:13:50,803
What do you think?

204
00:13:50,873 --> 00:13:52,803
It sounds like a great project.

205
00:13:52,873 --> 00:13:53,873
Yes.

206
00:13:53,943 --> 00:13:55,603
And now that I'm seeing you in person.

207
00:13:55,673 --> 00:13:56,743
CEO Ji,

208
00:13:56,843 --> 00:13:59,283
you're much more handsome than in your photos.

209
00:13:59,813 --> 00:14:04,053
Why haven't you ever been on television before?

210
00:14:05,683 --> 00:14:09,553
Right? Our CEO Ji is even more handsome in person.

211
00:14:12,423 --> 00:14:13,523
Well,

212
00:14:13,823 --> 00:14:18,093
CEO Ji is a little introverted.

213
00:14:18,963 --> 00:14:22,903
- Could CEO Baek go on by herself... - No.

214
00:14:23,303 --> 00:14:25,433
I absolutely need both of you to be on the show.

215
00:14:27,073 --> 00:14:29,143
Both of us?

216
00:14:29,373 --> 00:14:31,073
Yes. The program's content...

217
00:14:31,143 --> 00:14:33,083
is about couples' stories, so we're looking...

218
00:14:33,143 --> 00:14:34,913
for a married couple to be on the show.

219
00:14:35,613 --> 00:14:36,613
I see.

220
00:14:36,683 --> 00:14:38,183
Yes, and in that regard,

221
00:14:38,653 --> 00:14:40,523
you two are the perfect fit.

222
00:14:40,783 --> 00:14:43,993
Besides, I hear you're a famously devoted couple.

223
00:14:50,833 --> 00:14:52,033
That's right.

224
00:14:52,093 --> 00:14:55,803
Our two CEOs are incredibly close.

225
00:14:56,003 --> 00:14:58,103
You've definitely come to the right place.

226
00:14:58,873 --> 00:15:02,913
Even lovebirds have nothing on them.

227
00:15:06,813 --> 00:15:09,553
So, will you give it some thought?

228
00:15:16,453 --> 00:15:17,553
(Free Fitting for Brides-To-Be)

229
00:15:17,623 --> 00:15:19,763
- Please watch your step. - Okay, thank you.

230
00:15:19,823 --> 00:15:21,163
- Goodbye. - Goodbye.

231
00:15:21,163 --> 00:15:22,523
- Take care. - You too.

232
00:15:24,533 --> 00:15:25,533
Hurry.

233
00:15:25,963 --> 00:15:27,033
I'm not doing it.

234
00:15:27,603 --> 00:15:28,663
Sir.

235
00:15:29,233 --> 00:15:30,833
Don't just say you won't do it.

236
00:15:31,133 --> 00:15:32,743
Try to be more positive about it.

237
00:15:32,873 --> 00:15:34,673
Positive or not, I can't do things like that.

238
00:15:34,743 --> 00:15:37,213
- I won't. - Why can't you do it?

239
00:15:37,543 --> 00:15:38,973
Not that I expected you to,

240
00:15:39,273 --> 00:15:41,443
but let's at least hear why. Why won't you do it?

241
00:15:43,353 --> 00:15:44,483
Because it's like being a clown.

242
00:15:44,653 --> 00:15:45,653
A clown?

243
00:15:45,913 --> 00:15:47,783
Pretending you agree when you don't, pretending you like things you hate,

244
00:15:47,853 --> 00:15:49,053
sucking up to people,

245
00:15:49,123 --> 00:15:50,523
and acting like a phony.

246
00:15:50,693 --> 00:15:51,993
What's that if not a clown?

247
00:15:52,653 --> 00:15:54,093
I don't want to stoop to that level.

248
00:15:57,293 --> 00:15:58,833
That is so you.

249
00:15:59,403 --> 00:16:00,663
You don't care what happens to the company...

250
00:16:00,763 --> 00:16:02,333
or if our employees starve.

251
00:16:02,403 --> 00:16:03,503
Even if your life depended on it, you...

252
00:16:03,573 --> 00:16:04,673
Even if my life depended on it, what?

253
00:16:04,733 --> 00:16:06,743
You'd still refuse to listen to anything I say.

254
00:16:06,803 --> 00:16:07,943
Just to be contrary.

255
00:16:08,843 --> 00:16:09,843
What?

256
00:16:10,773 --> 00:16:12,783
Let's just go inside, Mi Young.

257
00:16:12,843 --> 00:16:14,313
Stop acting so high and mighty.

258
00:16:14,383 --> 00:16:15,613
You think you own this company?

259
00:16:16,753 --> 00:16:17,783
Oh, no.

260
00:16:18,883 --> 00:16:19,883
Here we go.

261
00:16:21,983 --> 00:16:25,893
Hey. You think you're successful because you're so special?

262
00:16:26,163 --> 00:16:30,093
No, designers like you are a dime a dozen in this country.

263
00:16:30,393 --> 00:16:34,163
The Ji Won Ho brand name was built on me playing the clown.

264
00:16:34,233 --> 00:16:35,863
Do you get it? Do you have any idea?

265
00:16:36,303 --> 00:16:38,573
- Mi Young, stop. - And another thing,

266
00:16:38,633 --> 00:16:40,303
even a clown wouldn't wear those pants.

267
00:16:40,373 --> 00:16:43,643
- Your knees have holes, you idiot. - Stop it.

268
00:16:44,073 --> 00:16:46,883
- You really... - Just stop.

269
00:16:46,943 --> 00:16:48,913
- Hey. - Seriously.

270
00:16:55,383 --> 00:16:56,593
You scared me.

271
00:16:57,823 --> 00:16:58,853
What is all this?

272
00:16:59,053 --> 00:17:00,363
J&White's last quarter's...

273
00:17:00,423 --> 00:17:02,263
financial statements and sales summary.

274
00:17:02,623 --> 00:17:05,293
Ji Won Ho needs to see this. That company's sales are falling.

275
00:17:05,663 --> 00:17:07,833
Maybe he'll come to his senses if he sees it with his own eyes.

276
00:17:08,563 --> 00:17:09,633
But...

277
00:17:10,103 --> 00:17:11,233
do you think that will work?

278
00:17:12,573 --> 00:17:15,503
If you want to persuade him,

279
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:20,313
don't you think you need to humour him a little?

280
00:17:20,443 --> 00:17:22,313
How much more? What else is there?

281
00:17:22,983 --> 00:17:24,113
I've always put up with...

282
00:17:24,183 --> 00:17:25,813
Ji Won Ho and catered to his every whim.

283
00:17:27,123 --> 00:17:28,883
This is the last straw. I can't take it anymore.

284
00:17:34,763 --> 00:17:35,763
Yes.

285
00:17:35,893 --> 00:17:37,893
We've secured evidence of assault by the defendant,

286
00:17:37,963 --> 00:17:39,863
so we can take away his custody and parental rights.

287
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:41,033
Don't worry.

288
00:17:41,533 --> 00:17:44,203
I'll give you the details in person when we meet tomorrow.

289
00:17:44,773 --> 00:17:46,843
We can meet at the café by your house like last time, right?

290
00:17:51,573 --> 00:17:52,643
It's no trouble at all.

291
00:17:54,513 --> 00:17:56,983
I'm much more comfortable going there myself.

292
00:17:57,753 --> 00:17:58,753
And when it comes to evidence,

293
00:17:59,483 --> 00:18:01,353
I prefer to collect it myself.

294
00:18:05,353 --> 00:18:06,463
I'll see you tomorrow.

295
00:18:16,803 --> 00:18:17,873
Ms. Baek Mi Young.

296
00:18:21,703 --> 00:18:23,043
Chi Hyun.

297
00:18:23,573 --> 00:18:26,243
Hello. Fancy seeing you here.

298
00:18:26,383 --> 00:18:28,583
I know, right? You remember her, don't you?

299
00:18:28,643 --> 00:18:29,783
Our manager.

300
00:18:30,053 --> 00:18:31,653
Hello. I was the one...

301
00:18:31,883 --> 00:18:33,983
who helped you with your dress fitting.

302
00:18:34,083 --> 00:18:36,853
Of course, I remember. It was my dress of a lifetime.

303
00:18:37,523 --> 00:18:38,723
If I get the chance,

304
00:18:39,023 --> 00:18:40,793
I'll come back to renew it.

305
00:18:41,363 --> 00:18:43,433
- What? - Renew?

306
00:18:43,933 --> 00:18:45,463
I got divorced recently.

307
00:18:46,063 --> 00:18:47,133
I see.

308
00:18:48,003 --> 00:18:49,733
Oh my, I had no idea.

309
00:18:50,333 --> 00:18:51,903
Well, things like that happen.

310
00:18:52,373 --> 00:18:53,843
If you ever need me, give me a call.

311
00:18:53,903 --> 00:18:55,473
(Jeon Chi Hyun, Divorce Lawyer, Specialist in Affairs)

312
00:18:55,543 --> 00:18:58,113
I knew you were a lawyer, but...

313
00:18:58,313 --> 00:19:01,113
"Affairs"?

314
00:19:01,383 --> 00:19:03,383
Hey, what's with you? Read the room.

315
00:19:05,083 --> 00:19:07,083
Of course, it's best if nothing happens,

316
00:19:07,553 --> 00:19:08,983
but you never know with life.

317
00:19:10,093 --> 00:19:11,323
Well, I should get going.

318
00:19:17,793 --> 00:19:21,263
A newly divorced divorce lawyer.

319
00:19:23,003 --> 00:19:25,173
She seems really tough, don't you think, Mi Young?

320
00:19:25,233 --> 00:19:27,173
Still, hearing a former client got divorced,

321
00:19:27,373 --> 00:19:28,773
it just feels strange.

322
00:19:29,873 --> 00:19:31,443
I'm sure she had her reasons.

323
00:19:32,943 --> 00:19:34,043
Hey, sit down.

324
00:19:34,413 --> 00:19:38,153
- All right, let's drink up. - Okay, sure.

325
00:19:38,253 --> 00:19:40,753
- Cheers. - Darn Ji Won Ho.

326
00:19:42,423 --> 00:19:44,153
You went too far this time.

327
00:19:44,893 --> 00:19:46,193
Mi Young is working so hard...

328
00:19:46,293 --> 00:19:47,463
to save the company.

329
00:19:47,823 --> 00:19:49,263
Hey, I'm trying too.

330
00:19:49,323 --> 00:19:51,263
Do you have to make a big show of it to prove you're trying?

331
00:19:52,663 --> 00:19:53,763
You know, Kyung Tae,

332
00:19:53,833 --> 00:19:56,063
you tend to subtly take Baek Mi Young's side.

333
00:19:56,403 --> 00:19:59,073
- Whose side are you on? - What? That's so childish.

334
00:20:00,203 --> 00:20:03,113
Anyway, it's not like Mi Young was completely wrong.

335
00:20:03,173 --> 00:20:05,473
First of all, her tone is just insulting.

336
00:20:05,543 --> 00:20:07,143
It's not like I'm her subordinate or something.

337
00:20:07,743 --> 00:20:08,743
But...

338
00:20:09,143 --> 00:20:10,553
are you really not going to do that variety show?

339
00:20:10,613 --> 00:20:11,613
I'm not doing it.

340
00:20:11,683 --> 00:20:13,083
I'll never do it, not in a million years.

341
00:20:17,053 --> 00:20:19,693
I'm not asking her to walk on eggshells around me.

342
00:20:19,823 --> 00:20:21,363
At the very least, there should be a minimum of...

343
00:20:21,423 --> 00:20:23,493
respect between a husband and wife.

344
00:20:23,563 --> 00:20:26,663
She treats me with less respect than a stray dog.

345
00:20:27,803 --> 00:20:28,803
You two have been sleeping...

346
00:20:28,863 --> 00:20:30,233
in separate rooms for a while, right?

347
00:20:32,933 --> 00:20:34,103
Yes, for about three years now.

348
00:20:34,443 --> 00:20:35,773
Since you're sleeping in separate rooms,

349
00:20:35,843 --> 00:20:38,143
you don't have a chance to fix your relationship.

350
00:20:40,583 --> 00:20:41,843
If you're going to keep living like this,

351
00:20:42,683 --> 00:20:43,683
then wouldn't it...

352
00:20:44,913 --> 00:20:46,153
be better to get a divorce?

353
00:20:49,353 --> 00:20:52,553
I just mean, if that's the case, wouldn't it be better for you...

354
00:20:52,623 --> 00:20:53,893
to find your own happiness separately?

355
00:20:54,363 --> 00:20:55,693
Life's too short.

356
00:20:56,393 --> 00:20:57,433
Darn it.

357
00:21:00,833 --> 00:21:02,103
Darn it.

358
00:21:10,713 --> 00:21:12,943
Lately, I've been feeling like...

359
00:21:14,113 --> 00:21:18,083
no matter how fast or how long I run,

360
00:21:19,013 --> 00:21:20,983
I'm still stuck in the same place.

361
00:21:21,883 --> 00:21:24,523
Like you're on a treadmill?

362
00:21:25,293 --> 00:21:26,423
A treadmill?

363
00:21:27,693 --> 00:21:28,993
Yes, something like that.

364
00:21:32,163 --> 00:21:33,733
I want to go further,

365
00:21:34,263 --> 00:21:36,403
all the way to the finish line.

366
00:21:37,973 --> 00:21:39,073
It's because...

367
00:21:40,043 --> 00:21:42,603
you're too ambitious.

368
00:21:43,143 --> 00:21:46,143
You're always trying to do things better,

369
00:21:46,243 --> 00:21:49,443
and trying to make everything perfect.

370
00:21:51,213 --> 00:21:52,313
I guess so.

371
00:21:53,783 --> 00:21:56,423
Even if all my dreams came true right now,

372
00:21:58,223 --> 00:22:01,123
I'm sure I'd just develop a new longing.

373
00:22:03,533 --> 00:22:04,563
But, A Ri.

374
00:22:06,703 --> 00:22:07,703
I...

375
00:22:08,603 --> 00:22:10,873
I really want to launch my own brand.

376
00:22:12,403 --> 00:22:13,943
Not J&White,

377
00:22:15,443 --> 00:22:16,443
but Baek Mi Young.

378
00:22:17,143 --> 00:22:18,873
A brand with only my name on it.

379
00:22:20,043 --> 00:22:21,343
My very own brand.

380
00:22:23,683 --> 00:22:27,723
And I want to feel what it's like...

381
00:22:29,083 --> 00:22:30,623
to have a clear path ahead of me,

382
00:22:32,023 --> 00:22:33,193
Then go for it.

383
00:23:12,193 --> 00:23:13,203
CEO Baek.

384
00:23:13,503 --> 00:23:15,263
I'm the writer who visited you earlier.

385
00:23:15,833 --> 00:23:16,873
About casting CEO Ji,

386
00:23:16,933 --> 00:23:19,103
we really need a decision by the end of today.

387
00:23:19,633 --> 00:23:20,643
If he can't do it,

388
00:23:20,643 --> 00:23:23,043
we'll have to hurry and find another designer.

389
00:23:26,613 --> 00:23:28,183
Won Ho, the writer needs your decision by today...

390
00:23:28,183 --> 00:23:30,083
What's this about a birthday meal all of a sudden?

391
00:23:30,413 --> 00:23:32,653
I'll just send you double your allowance.

392
00:23:33,423 --> 00:23:35,053
I don't know. Then you can call Mi Young,

393
00:23:35,123 --> 00:23:36,853
and talk to her yourself.

394
00:23:37,023 --> 00:23:38,253
I don't know. I'm hanging up.

395
00:23:38,723 --> 00:23:40,393
She's acting like a child.

396
00:23:42,063 --> 00:23:43,123
You startled me.

397
00:23:43,863 --> 00:23:44,863
When did you get here?

398
00:23:44,933 --> 00:23:45,963
Just now.

399
00:23:47,263 --> 00:23:49,703
What was that call about?

400
00:23:50,033 --> 00:23:52,503
It was my mom. Her birthday is coming up.

401
00:23:53,133 --> 00:23:54,873
She's suddenly asking for a birthday meal.

402
00:23:55,303 --> 00:23:56,473
A birthday meal from her daughter-in-law...

403
00:23:56,543 --> 00:23:57,673
is her biggest wish or something.

404
00:23:58,173 --> 00:23:59,173
I see.

405
00:24:00,813 --> 00:24:02,313
Forget it. Don't worry about it.

406
00:24:02,383 --> 00:24:04,283
It's not the first time my mom has made a fuss.

407
00:24:06,783 --> 00:24:08,323
I really should just turn this off.

408
00:24:11,023 --> 00:24:13,893
If you want to persuade him,

409
00:24:13,963 --> 00:24:19,293
don't you think you need to humour him a little?

410
00:24:21,433 --> 00:24:23,633
- I'll do it. - Okay.

411
00:24:25,203 --> 00:24:26,473
What? Do what?

412
00:24:26,533 --> 00:24:28,503
Making the birthday meal for your mother.

413
00:24:28,703 --> 00:24:29,703
I'll do it.

414
00:24:29,803 --> 00:24:30,813
What are you talking about?

415
00:24:30,873 --> 00:24:31,873
Why would you do that all of a sudden?

416
00:24:31,943 --> 00:24:33,683
Forget it. That's weird. Don't do it.

417
00:24:33,883 --> 00:24:35,413
No, what's weird about it?

418
00:24:35,483 --> 00:24:37,913
A daughter-in-law making a meal for her mother-in-law's birthday.

419
00:24:40,253 --> 00:24:41,753
You're just doing this because of that, aren't you?

420
00:24:42,453 --> 00:24:45,623
- What? - This won't make me go on the show.

421
00:24:45,753 --> 00:24:46,763
That's not it.

422
00:24:46,863 --> 00:24:48,523
I've always wanted...

423
00:24:48,593 --> 00:24:50,433
to make a birthday meal for her.

424
00:24:51,593 --> 00:24:54,203
I've been too neglectful of her until now.

425
00:24:54,603 --> 00:24:57,673
As her daughter-in-law, it's the right thing to do.

426
00:25:06,713 --> 00:25:07,743
Good grief.

427
00:25:08,313 --> 00:25:09,543
Hello, Mother.

428
00:25:09,543 --> 00:25:10,783
Hello, Seung Ho.

429
00:25:11,083 --> 00:25:12,213
Hi, Ha Neul.

430
00:25:12,383 --> 00:25:13,983
Aunt Mi Young.

431
00:25:14,253 --> 00:25:15,923
Oh, Mi Young, you really came?

432
00:25:16,423 --> 00:25:17,423
Yes, I did.

433
00:25:17,953 --> 00:25:19,793
Mom, what are you doing? Mi Young is saying hello.

434
00:25:20,623 --> 00:25:23,993
Mi Young, you're going to make me a birthday meal yourself?

435
00:25:24,593 --> 00:25:26,193
Yes. It's nothing special,

436
00:25:26,263 --> 00:25:27,863
but I brought some things to prepare.

437
00:25:28,303 --> 00:25:30,503
Well then, let's see what you can do.

438
00:25:30,573 --> 00:25:32,373
I can help with that...

439
00:25:34,303 --> 00:25:36,303
Your back is acting up, what are you trying to do?

440
00:25:36,443 --> 00:25:37,643
You need to rest.

441
00:25:38,443 --> 00:25:41,213
- It's okay. I'll help. - Oh, Won Ho.

442
00:25:41,813 --> 00:25:43,683
Go to my room and alter one of my dresses for me.

443
00:25:43,813 --> 00:25:46,783
I've gained weight, and the hem's completely torn.

444
00:25:46,853 --> 00:25:49,623
Fix your dress? Out of the blue?

445
00:25:49,683 --> 00:25:52,253
Please, just fix it. I have nothing to wear.

446
00:25:52,323 --> 00:25:54,563
Come here. Fix my dress.

447
00:25:55,623 --> 00:25:57,433
I have nothing to wear.

448
00:25:58,763 --> 00:26:01,303
I'm sorry about that.

449
00:26:01,803 --> 00:26:04,473
Ha Neul, let's go. Let's get something to drink.

450
00:26:09,473 --> 00:26:12,343
Okay, where should I start?

451
00:26:52,783 --> 00:26:54,323
You should throw things like this out.

452
00:26:55,723 --> 00:26:56,923
This is nice.

453
00:26:56,993 --> 00:26:58,793
(Mystery)

454
00:27:01,193 --> 00:27:02,363
What's that smell?

455
00:27:03,323 --> 00:27:05,663
Is Mi Young cooking?

456
00:27:08,563 --> 00:27:10,103
Smells delicious.

457
00:27:56,183 --> 00:27:57,183
Hey.

458
00:27:58,113 --> 00:27:59,853
Did you just throw that?

459
00:28:03,053 --> 00:28:04,693
There are some things you just don't throw.

460
00:28:06,523 --> 00:28:08,593
If you don't want to do this, just say so.

461
00:28:08,763 --> 00:28:12,463
No, Mother. It was an accident...

462
00:28:15,733 --> 00:28:16,733
Listen.

463
00:28:17,503 --> 00:28:19,203
Have you given up on having a child?

464
00:28:19,803 --> 00:28:20,803
Pardon?

465
00:28:20,903 --> 00:28:23,873
Why are you so skinny?

466
00:28:23,973 --> 00:28:26,473
You look even thinner than last time.

467
00:28:27,183 --> 00:28:28,613
Don't tell me you've given up...

468
00:28:28,683 --> 00:28:30,613
just because you failed once, have you?

469
00:28:32,553 --> 00:28:35,183
You need some meat on your bones to get pregnant.

470
00:28:35,453 --> 00:28:37,293
Just because you're the same age as Won Ho,

471
00:28:37,353 --> 00:28:39,523
you can't think you're the same as him. Okay?

472
00:28:39,653 --> 00:28:42,793
A man can have children until the day he dies.

473
00:28:43,123 --> 00:28:44,433
But a woman...

474
00:28:45,093 --> 00:28:47,363
I don't have to spell it out, do I?

475
00:28:51,033 --> 00:28:54,273
A child who looks like Won Ho would be so smart and beautiful.

476
00:29:24,303 --> 00:29:28,273
- Ha Neul, did you pick a book? - Yes. Please read me this one.

477
00:29:28,343 --> 00:29:30,473
Okay, bring it here.

478
00:29:32,243 --> 00:29:33,683
(The Butterfly's Dream)

479
00:29:34,013 --> 00:29:35,883
Okay.

480
00:29:36,713 --> 00:29:38,253
But Auntie,

481
00:29:38,353 --> 00:29:40,323
are your clothes too small for you too?

482
00:29:40,483 --> 00:29:42,483
Huh? What do you mean?

483
00:29:42,623 --> 00:29:44,893
Just now, you were breathing...

484
00:29:48,363 --> 00:29:50,063
like this.

485
00:29:51,193 --> 00:29:54,833
That's a trick I use when I'm feeling upset.

486
00:29:54,903 --> 00:29:56,203
If you take a deep breath...

487
00:29:57,233 --> 00:29:58,833
like this,

488
00:30:00,033 --> 00:30:01,443
and then let it all out,

489
00:30:02,203 --> 00:30:04,143
it helps you feel a little better.

490
00:30:05,213 --> 00:30:07,283
But what did you mean about my clothes being too small?

491
00:30:07,513 --> 00:30:09,883
When I used to live with my mom,

492
00:30:09,943 --> 00:30:12,553
she used to do that too, just like you.

493
00:30:12,713 --> 00:30:14,083
Back then, my mom said...

494
00:30:14,153 --> 00:30:16,993
it was because she was wearing clothes that didn't fit her.

495
00:30:17,423 --> 00:30:20,463
She said it was hard to breathe.

496
00:30:23,223 --> 00:30:27,933
You're right. I guess my clothes are too small for me too.

497
00:30:40,583 --> 00:30:45,053
- You’re really out to get me today. - Well, you should visit more often,

498
00:30:45,353 --> 00:30:46,653
if it weren't for my birthday,

499
00:30:46,713 --> 00:30:50,693
- wouldn't have thought of coming? - I've been busy, that's why.

500
00:30:50,753 --> 00:30:52,823
Oh, please. That's always your excuse.

501
00:30:52,923 --> 00:30:54,593
You think I have time to spare?

502
00:30:55,423 --> 00:30:56,723
But I'm here now, aren't I?

503
00:30:56,793 --> 00:30:59,733
And we brought all this to make you a birthday dinner.

504
00:30:59,793 --> 00:31:02,933
Please, I practically had to beg you, you brat. Right?

505
00:31:03,063 --> 00:31:04,403
Other people's sons...

506
00:31:04,473 --> 00:31:06,633
get married and are well supported by their in-laws.

507
00:31:08,273 --> 00:31:09,443
Oh, not this again.

508
00:31:09,503 --> 00:31:11,113
What are you trying to say?

509
00:31:11,173 --> 00:31:12,273
It's just...

510
00:31:12,343 --> 00:31:13,883
I feel sorry for you.

511
00:31:14,383 --> 00:31:16,143
You never even met your in-laws.

512
00:31:16,883 --> 00:31:19,583
I mean, how could they die so tragically like that?

513
00:31:21,383 --> 00:31:22,723
Mom, be honest.

514
00:31:22,983 --> 00:31:24,293
This birthday dinner is just an excuse, isn't it?

515
00:31:25,323 --> 00:31:26,323
What?

516
00:31:26,393 --> 00:31:28,823
You're just doing this to give Mi Young a hard time.

517
00:31:28,893 --> 00:31:30,693
Because you don't like her.

518
00:31:31,833 --> 00:31:33,903
But why do you dislike her so much?

519
00:31:33,963 --> 00:31:35,563
What has she ever done that was so wrong?

520
00:31:35,633 --> 00:31:38,433
What are you talking about? Don't be ridiculous.

521
00:31:38,503 --> 00:31:40,543
She's your daughter-in-law, not a stranger.

522
00:31:40,603 --> 00:31:42,343
Can't you just try to like her a little?

523
00:31:42,403 --> 00:31:43,403
Quiet.

524
00:31:44,873 --> 00:31:47,583
By the way, why haven't you two had a baby?

525
00:31:48,143 --> 00:31:49,313
Where did that come from?

526
00:31:49,843 --> 00:31:51,083
Tell me the truth.

527
00:31:51,213 --> 00:31:53,513
Is it Mi Young who doesn't want to have one?

528
00:31:53,583 --> 00:31:56,823
- That's it, isn't it? - That's not it.

529
00:31:57,023 --> 00:31:59,853
And if you keep this up, we'll never have a baby.

530
00:32:00,093 --> 00:32:01,093
What?

531
00:32:01,163 --> 00:32:04,093
I'm not doing this. You do it, Mom. This is so frustrating. Darn it.

532
00:32:04,863 --> 00:32:06,563
- Hey. - I knew this would happen.

533
00:32:06,633 --> 00:32:10,033
Hey, say that again.

534
00:32:10,373 --> 00:32:12,333
What did I possibly do to keep you two from having a baby?

535
00:32:12,403 --> 00:32:15,403
It's true. You're always stressing us out over things like this,

536
00:32:15,473 --> 00:32:16,943
so when would we ever have time to have a baby?

537
00:32:17,003 --> 00:32:18,573
Have you quite finished, you little brat?

538
00:32:18,743 --> 00:32:20,883
How have I been stressing you out?

539
00:32:23,083 --> 00:32:25,313
What's going on now? What's this all about?

540
00:32:25,453 --> 00:32:26,853
Mi Young, did you say that to Won Ho,

541
00:32:27,253 --> 00:32:29,423
that you're not getting pregnant because I'm stressing you out?

542
00:32:29,423 --> 00:32:30,423
Excuse me?

543
00:32:30,423 --> 00:32:31,493
If you hadn't said anything,

544
00:32:31,493 --> 00:32:32,623
why would he say something like that?

545
00:32:32,693 --> 00:32:33,693
Stop it.

546
00:32:36,293 --> 00:32:37,833
Because you always act like this,

547
00:32:37,893 --> 00:32:40,433
this is why I hate coming to this house. Got it?

548
00:32:40,503 --> 00:32:41,703
What did you say, you brat?

549
00:32:42,403 --> 00:32:44,703
- Won Ho, stop it. - Hey, Won Ho.

550
00:32:44,773 --> 00:32:45,803
You shouldn't say that.

551
00:32:45,873 --> 00:32:49,273
What do you mean? Every time I come, she's dying to pick a fight.

552
00:32:49,373 --> 00:32:52,173
Get out. Get out of my house right now, you brat.

553
00:32:52,243 --> 00:32:55,113
- Fine, I was leaving anyway. - Hey.

554
00:32:55,183 --> 00:32:58,183
- Goodbye. - Hey, Won Ho.

555
00:32:58,313 --> 00:32:59,313
Hey, Won Ho.

556
00:33:00,983 --> 00:33:01,983
Hey, Won Ho...

557
00:33:02,523 --> 00:33:03,523
Mom...

558
00:33:03,853 --> 00:33:06,853
Just you dare come back to my house. You little brat.

559
00:33:06,923 --> 00:33:08,963
- Mom, come on. - That little brat.

560
00:33:11,333 --> 00:33:12,633
That little brat.

561
00:33:19,103 --> 00:33:20,503
Did you really have to do that?

562
00:33:21,943 --> 00:33:22,943
Do what?

563
00:33:23,203 --> 00:33:24,473
To your mother.

564
00:33:25,143 --> 00:33:27,113
It's her birthday, after all.

565
00:33:27,913 --> 00:33:29,343
So, what? Should I have said we're having a baby?

566
00:33:29,683 --> 00:33:31,313
That we'll give her a grandchild right away?

567
00:33:33,353 --> 00:33:35,423
That's why when my mom starts saying strange things,

568
00:33:35,483 --> 00:33:36,583
don't just stand there and take it.

569
00:33:36,653 --> 00:33:38,653
You need to be firm about your feelings.

570
00:33:38,723 --> 00:33:40,423
Because you're always so focused on your image,

571
00:33:40,493 --> 00:33:42,763
my mom thinks she can walk all over you.

572
00:33:42,993 --> 00:33:45,093
You have no problem arguing back with me.

573
00:33:45,893 --> 00:33:47,363
If this was going to happen, why did you even go?

574
00:33:47,503 --> 00:33:49,763
I told you not to go there. We went here for no reason,

575
00:33:49,833 --> 00:33:51,473
and got nothing out of it. So what was the point?

576
00:33:53,173 --> 00:33:54,173
Hey.

577
00:33:55,403 --> 00:33:58,573
What is wrong with you? Hey.

578
00:33:59,613 --> 00:34:02,713
Stop! Darn it. Hey. Hey, Baek Mi Young.

579
00:34:05,653 --> 00:34:06,753
Hey, Baek Mi Young.

580
00:34:07,223 --> 00:34:09,923
What is wrong with you? Hey!

581
00:34:30,743 --> 00:34:32,613
- Pull over. - What?

582
00:34:33,313 --> 00:34:35,813
- I said, pull over. - Why?

583
00:34:46,653 --> 00:34:48,723
What are you trying to do?

584
00:34:55,503 --> 00:34:56,503
Come on.

585
00:35:02,443 --> 00:35:04,013
Gosh...

586
00:35:08,013 --> 00:35:09,013
Looks like your wife went all out...

587
00:35:09,083 --> 00:35:10,083
on the birthday feast before she left.

588
00:35:10,513 --> 00:35:12,183
Hey, who is going to eat all this?

589
00:35:12,713 --> 00:35:14,923
Anyway, tell your wife I said thanks.

590
00:35:37,443 --> 00:35:39,473
That's why when my mom starts saying strange things,

591
00:35:39,543 --> 00:35:40,613
don't just stand there and take it.

592
00:35:40,683 --> 00:35:42,683
You need to be firm about your feelings.

593
00:35:43,013 --> 00:35:45,053
You have no problem arguing back with me.

594
00:35:45,213 --> 00:35:47,013
Just because you're the same age as Won Ho,

595
00:35:47,083 --> 00:35:49,183
you can't think you're the same as him. Okay?

596
00:35:49,523 --> 00:35:52,293
A man can have children until the day he dies.

597
00:35:52,353 --> 00:35:54,223
Mi Young, did you say that to Won Ho,

598
00:35:54,463 --> 00:35:56,593
that you're not getting pregnant because I'm stressing you out?

599
00:35:56,893 --> 00:35:58,963
- Excuse me? - If you hadn't said anything,

600
00:35:59,033 --> 00:36:00,063
why would he say something like that?

601
00:36:36,063 --> 00:36:37,373
Please look a little to your left.

602
00:36:37,933 --> 00:36:38,933
Okay.

603
00:36:42,443 --> 00:36:45,713
- Those details really pop outdoors. - Looks good.

604
00:36:47,073 --> 00:36:48,083
Wait a minute.

605
00:36:50,383 --> 00:36:52,413
Those details and the colour really stand out.

606
00:36:57,523 --> 00:36:59,353
- Looks good. - Great.

607
00:36:59,423 --> 00:37:01,263
This is great.

608
00:37:01,523 --> 00:37:02,523
Yes.

609
00:37:08,133 --> 00:37:09,503
(Mi Young)

610
00:37:09,563 --> 00:37:10,903
Come straight home when you're done.

611
00:37:11,533 --> 00:37:12,603
We need to talk.

612
00:37:19,513 --> 00:37:21,183
The scenery is great,

613
00:37:21,343 --> 00:37:23,243
the photos are great, and the concept is great.

614
00:37:27,453 --> 00:37:28,983
I haven't told him yet.

615
00:37:29,253 --> 00:37:31,853
What are you going to do if you still haven't told him?

616
00:37:32,193 --> 00:37:35,163
I kept meaning to tell him, but I never got the chance.

617
00:37:35,593 --> 00:37:37,633
How are you going to deal with the fallout from this?

618
00:37:39,263 --> 00:37:41,333
Actually, when he gets home today,

619
00:37:41,663 --> 00:37:44,033
I'm going to talk to him and convince him to do the reality show.

620
00:37:44,633 --> 00:37:47,103
It won't be easy, but good luck.

621
00:37:47,843 --> 00:37:49,703
Okay. I'll call you back later.

622
00:37:50,203 --> 00:37:51,213
Okay.

623
00:37:57,813 --> 00:38:00,513
- Hello. - Am I speaking with Baek Mi Young?

624
00:38:01,423 --> 00:38:02,623
Yes, this is she.

625
00:38:03,223 --> 00:38:04,653
This is Maesan Hospital.

626
00:38:05,523 --> 00:38:07,563
Your husband is unconscious right now...

627
00:38:11,533 --> 00:38:14,133
These phone scammers are getting really creative.

628
00:38:23,943 --> 00:38:27,073
(Mother-In-Law's Son)

629
00:38:29,713 --> 00:38:31,013
The person you have called is unavailable...

630
00:38:31,013 --> 00:38:32,653
and will be connected to voicemail.

631
00:38:33,113 --> 00:38:34,623
Please leave your message after the tone...

632
00:38:35,123 --> 00:38:37,553
(Vice President Kang)

633
00:38:42,193 --> 00:38:45,233
Yes, Kyung Tae. Are you with Won Ho right now?

634
00:38:45,633 --> 00:38:48,133
No, he went home a while ago.

635
00:38:48,963 --> 00:38:50,063
He left a long time ago.

636
00:38:50,803 --> 00:38:51,803
Okay.

637
00:39:30,873 --> 00:39:32,313
(Mother-In-Law's Son)

638
00:39:32,373 --> 00:39:33,373
(Calling Mother-In-Law's Son)

639
00:39:36,583 --> 00:39:38,913
The person you have called is unavailable...

640
00:39:39,183 --> 00:39:40,583
(Vice President Kang)

641
00:39:40,653 --> 00:39:42,223
(Calling Vice President Kang)

642
00:39:42,623 --> 00:39:46,123
Kyung Tae, can you find out where Won Ho is right now?

643
00:39:47,153 --> 00:39:49,593
If you get in touch with Won Ho, please give me a call.

644
00:39:50,493 --> 00:39:51,493
(Vice President Kang)

645
00:39:54,503 --> 00:39:55,863
This is Maesan Hospital.

646
00:39:57,003 --> 00:39:59,073
Your husband is unconscious right now...

647
00:40:19,893 --> 00:40:21,893
(Maesan Hospital Emergency Medical Center)

648
00:40:46,513 --> 00:40:47,513
Please move out of the way.

649
00:42:06,893 --> 00:42:09,563
Daddy's right here, so don't worry.

650
00:42:10,463 --> 00:42:13,073
Daddy will protect our princesses.

651
00:42:13,133 --> 00:42:14,603
Kiss.

652
00:42:44,403 --> 00:42:45,833
He says he’s at the fishing spot right now.

653
00:42:46,473 --> 00:42:48,573
I just spoke with him, so don't worry.

654
00:43:19,533 --> 00:43:21,703
(3 Years Ago)

655
00:43:38,353 --> 00:43:40,553
- Honey. - What?

656
00:43:41,663 --> 00:43:42,663
Why?

657
00:43:43,923 --> 00:43:45,933
What is it? Were you having a nightmare?

658
00:43:50,333 --> 00:43:54,103
Yes, something terrifying was chasing me.

659
00:43:55,503 --> 00:43:58,973
I tried to run away, but my feet were stuck.

660
00:44:00,213 --> 00:44:01,413
It was so scary.

661
00:44:01,613 --> 00:44:04,713
You should have called for me.

662
00:44:05,583 --> 00:44:06,853
You're all sweaty.

663
00:44:13,393 --> 00:44:14,393
Ta-da.

664
00:44:15,693 --> 00:44:18,433
Were you scared, Princess Dallae?

665
00:44:19,533 --> 00:44:22,103
Daddy's right here, so don't worry.

666
00:44:23,563 --> 00:44:26,173
Daddy will protect our princesses.

667
00:44:26,233 --> 00:44:27,843
Kiss.

668
00:44:33,673 --> 00:44:34,983
Are you leaving for work already?

669
00:44:35,783 --> 00:44:38,053
Yes, I have a lot to do today. I have to go out for work.

670
00:44:38,483 --> 00:44:41,283
- You get more rest and come later. - You're going out for work?

671
00:44:42,123 --> 00:44:44,283
Yes, with Ms. Kwon.

672
00:44:44,653 --> 00:44:45,653
What?

673
00:44:48,223 --> 00:44:50,563
So I have to close up by myself again today?

674
00:44:51,663 --> 00:44:54,063
I'm sorry. Today's the last day. It will all be over today.

675
00:44:54,663 --> 00:44:58,703
How many times have you said that? I seriously want to cry.

676
00:44:59,203 --> 00:45:01,203
I know. I thought it would be over sooner too,

677
00:45:01,343 --> 00:45:02,603
but it's taking longer than expected.

678
00:45:03,743 --> 00:45:04,843
But honey,

679
00:45:06,073 --> 00:45:09,683
can't you please not go today?

680
00:45:10,183 --> 00:45:13,113
I'm feeling anxious because of the dream I had.

681
00:45:13,183 --> 00:45:17,023
- I don't feel well either. - Today is the last day.

682
00:45:19,553 --> 00:45:22,163
So to you,

683
00:45:22,623 --> 00:45:24,463
Ms. Kwon is more important than me and Dallae.

684
00:45:25,433 --> 00:45:26,593
How can you say that?

685
00:45:26,663 --> 00:45:28,863
Who do you think I'm working this hard for?

686
00:45:31,103 --> 00:45:32,803
I'm making wedding attire for multicultural couples...

687
00:45:32,873 --> 00:45:34,433
who are struggling financially.

688
00:45:34,603 --> 00:45:37,203
And Ms. Kwon said she would do a lot of promotion for us.

689
00:45:37,473 --> 00:45:40,813
But it's just too hard for me to do it alone without you.

690
00:45:42,313 --> 00:45:44,753
Then just leave anything that's too difficult.

691
00:45:44,983 --> 00:45:46,813
I'll come back as soon as I can and finish up.

692
00:45:49,623 --> 00:45:51,153
Honey, please,

693
00:45:51,423 --> 00:45:54,863
don't go today. Please?

694
00:46:08,343 --> 00:46:09,443
Yes, hello?

695
00:46:10,103 --> 00:46:13,773
Yes, I'm sorry. It's not ready yet.

696
00:46:14,943 --> 00:46:17,713
Five meters of lace.

697
00:46:19,083 --> 00:46:20,713
- Lace. - And...

698
00:46:22,023 --> 00:46:23,923
ten bolts of silk.

699
00:46:28,363 --> 00:46:30,563
Don't overdo it. Just leave anything that's too difficult,

700
00:46:30,623 --> 00:46:32,093
and I'll do it as soon as I get back.

701
00:46:32,733 --> 00:46:33,833
I'll be right back, okay?

702
00:46:33,933 --> 00:46:34,933
I'll be back soon.

703
00:46:57,883 --> 00:47:00,093
Hello, Ms. Kwon. I'm on my way now.

704
00:47:48,043 --> 00:47:51,673
(Operating Room)

705
00:48:33,313 --> 00:48:35,523
I'm so sorry, but the baby...

706
00:48:56,503 --> 00:48:57,843
You should just rest.

707
00:49:04,113 --> 00:49:05,113
Don't throw it away.

708
00:49:05,413 --> 00:49:07,583
- Just leave it. - No.

709
00:49:10,553 --> 00:49:13,123
Looking at it will just be a painful reminder.

710
00:49:47,223 --> 00:49:48,493
Don't get sentimental.

711
00:49:49,623 --> 00:49:51,323
You don't have the right.

712
00:49:55,103 --> 00:49:56,663
Now that Dallae's gone,

713
00:49:57,763 --> 00:49:59,373
there's nothing holding you back anymore.

714
00:50:01,133 --> 00:50:03,473
You can do whatever you like now.

715
00:50:04,673 --> 00:50:05,673
What?

716
00:50:06,513 --> 00:50:08,783
You can even do all the volunteering you want.

717
00:50:09,683 --> 00:50:11,113
How can you say that right now?

718
00:50:13,883 --> 00:50:15,353
When we lost Dallae,

719
00:50:16,953 --> 00:50:18,553
you weren't there for us.

720
00:50:20,153 --> 00:50:21,153
I...

721
00:50:23,393 --> 00:50:25,163
I was all alone again.

722
00:50:31,933 --> 00:50:32,933
That day...

723
00:50:34,033 --> 00:50:35,403
From that morning,

724
00:50:37,073 --> 00:50:41,683
something felt so wrong. I felt so anxious.

725
00:50:42,183 --> 00:50:43,783
I told you not to go.

726
00:50:45,353 --> 00:50:47,183
I begged you not to leave.

727
00:50:49,583 --> 00:50:50,583
Dallae.

728
00:50:51,653 --> 00:50:53,093
It's your fault this happened.

729
00:50:53,353 --> 00:50:55,563
How was I supposed to know every detail about your condition?

730
00:50:55,623 --> 00:50:56,863
The baby was inside you.

731
00:50:57,563 --> 00:50:58,563
What?

732
00:50:59,763 --> 00:51:01,333
Inside me?

733
00:51:03,203 --> 00:51:04,203
No.

734
00:51:05,303 --> 00:51:06,303
I...

735
00:51:06,873 --> 00:51:08,103
I still...

736
00:51:08,903 --> 00:51:11,713
I still feel like Dallae is right here.

737
00:51:12,713 --> 00:51:15,713
I feel like she's still here playing.

738
00:51:19,653 --> 00:51:20,883
It feels like if I just wait a little longer,

739
00:51:20,953 --> 00:51:22,983
I'll be able to see her.

740
00:51:28,093 --> 00:51:29,093
Mi Young.

741
00:51:29,493 --> 00:51:32,763
- Give that to me. I'll... - No. This...

742
00:51:33,033 --> 00:51:35,533
This is our Dallae's toy.

743
00:51:36,233 --> 00:51:38,503
It's her toy. I can't let her go.

744
00:51:39,733 --> 00:51:43,303
Mommy is so sorry. I'm so sorry I couldn't protect you.

745
00:51:43,873 --> 00:51:44,873
Mommy...

746
00:51:46,243 --> 00:51:47,343
Dallae...

747
00:51:48,813 --> 00:51:49,883
I'm so sorry.

748
00:52:33,623 --> 00:52:34,853
What are you doing sitting in the dark?

749
00:52:42,863 --> 00:52:45,833
Well, the weather was so nice for a change.

750
00:52:47,603 --> 00:52:49,603
And I happened to be near a freshwater fishing spot.

751
00:52:49,673 --> 00:52:51,643
I even caught a fish. A really big one. Want to see it?

752
00:52:52,413 --> 00:52:53,773
Why didn't you answer your phone?

753
00:52:57,683 --> 00:53:00,613
You told me to come straight home. If I answered, you'd nag...

754
00:53:04,323 --> 00:53:06,123
I knew you'd just yell at me.

755
00:53:07,393 --> 00:53:09,623
So 26 missed calls...

756
00:53:10,663 --> 00:53:12,433
just looked like me nagging you?

757
00:53:15,103 --> 00:53:16,103
I'm sorry.

758
00:53:32,213 --> 00:53:34,383
(Dream Project: Wedding Edition)

759
00:53:41,423 --> 00:53:42,863
I don't think I can hear it.

760
00:53:43,123 --> 00:53:45,793
Isn't CEO Baek incredible?

761
00:53:46,763 --> 00:53:47,763
She got CEO Ji...

762
00:53:47,833 --> 00:53:48,833
who swore he'd never do a variety show.

763
00:53:49,163 --> 00:53:53,673
- How did she convince him? - Oh, don't even get me started.

764
00:53:54,073 --> 00:53:56,203
My stomach was in knots just watching.

765
00:53:57,303 --> 00:53:59,543
What? Your stomach was in knots?

766
00:54:00,173 --> 00:54:03,213
It's an expression.

767
00:54:04,843 --> 00:54:05,853
Hello.

768
00:54:05,853 --> 00:54:07,313
Oh, I'm so sorry. The weather's so cold,

769
00:54:07,383 --> 00:54:08,823
and we ended up having to shoot outdoors.

770
00:54:08,883 --> 00:54:12,023
We can handle a little cold. Right, CEO Ji?

771
00:54:13,353 --> 00:54:14,923
Oh, yes. I'm fine as well.

772
00:54:16,293 --> 00:54:18,633
We would've preferred to shoot indoors,

773
00:54:18,863 --> 00:54:21,703
but the participant's dream is to have a wedding on a boat.

774
00:54:22,163 --> 00:54:23,703
In any case, we look forward to working with you.

775
00:54:24,033 --> 00:54:25,033
Of course.

776
00:54:26,803 --> 00:54:29,773
You put all this together in just one day?

777
00:54:29,843 --> 00:54:32,073
It looks like it would've taken a long time.

778
00:54:32,813 --> 00:54:33,813
Excuse me?

779
00:54:33,873 --> 00:54:35,313
Oh, we couldn't do it in just one day.

780
00:54:35,683 --> 00:54:37,343
It took us several days just to secure the boat.

781
00:54:38,013 --> 00:54:39,013
What?

782
00:54:39,583 --> 00:54:41,753
This is all thanks to the two of you.

783
00:54:42,183 --> 00:54:44,253
Because you agreed to our offer on the day I approached you,

784
00:54:44,323 --> 00:54:46,093
we were able to line up our filming schedule perfectly.

785
00:54:47,053 --> 00:54:48,053
What did you say?

786
00:54:49,163 --> 00:54:51,163
Yes, are we heading to the shoot now?

787
00:54:51,223 --> 00:54:52,893
Wait a minute. What is this all about?

788
00:54:53,293 --> 00:54:56,263
We agreed on the day we were asked? I only said I would do it yesterday.

789
00:54:56,903 --> 00:54:57,933
Oh, about that...

790
00:55:00,403 --> 00:55:01,403
I'm sorry.

791
00:55:01,573 --> 00:55:05,273
I told her beforehand that we'd do it.

792
00:55:05,713 --> 00:55:07,413
I was going to tell you later.

793
00:55:09,743 --> 00:55:12,283
So, shall we get going?

794
00:55:12,353 --> 00:55:14,253
- Yes. - No.

795
00:55:14,913 --> 00:55:16,023
I'm not doing the shoot.

796
00:55:19,653 --> 00:55:21,793
CEO Baek, you're really going too far now.

797
00:55:22,323 --> 00:55:24,393
So have you been lying to me this whole time?

798
00:55:25,933 --> 00:55:27,093
What's wrong with you? People are watching.

799
00:55:27,163 --> 00:55:28,163
Keep your voice down.

800
00:55:28,233 --> 00:55:29,963
And what if I don't?

801
00:55:30,163 --> 00:55:31,403
Everyone here deserves to know...

802
00:55:31,463 --> 00:55:33,503
how you tricked me and do what you want.

803
00:55:42,483 --> 00:55:43,483
It's just...

804
00:55:44,913 --> 00:55:48,083
I didn't mean to trick you from the beginning.

805
00:55:48,413 --> 00:55:50,523
I just missed the right time to tell you.

806
00:55:50,653 --> 00:55:52,753
Oh, you missed the right time? Why?

807
00:55:52,893 --> 00:55:54,523
You might as well say you sent it telepathically.

808
00:55:54,593 --> 00:55:56,263
It's true, really.

809
00:55:56,423 --> 00:55:58,593
No, Won Ho, you never gave me a chance to talk.

810
00:55:58,663 --> 00:56:00,433
Oh, cut the act. Seriously.

811
00:56:01,293 --> 00:56:02,803
Your mom's birthday dinner,

812
00:56:02,863 --> 00:56:04,533
the 26 calls you made yesterday,

813
00:56:04,603 --> 00:56:06,033
it was all an act, wasn't it?

814
00:56:06,103 --> 00:56:07,573
You knew that I'd get weak...

815
00:56:07,633 --> 00:56:09,373
and give you permission. You calculated it all.

816
00:56:09,443 --> 00:56:10,773
You already had the answer you wanted...

817
00:56:10,843 --> 00:56:12,573
and made a fool out of me, didn't you?

818
00:56:12,643 --> 00:56:15,143
That wasn't entirely about the show.

819
00:56:15,213 --> 00:56:18,813
- This is really annoying. - No, Won Ho.

820
00:56:18,883 --> 00:56:19,983
Hey, Won Ho.

821
00:56:23,883 --> 00:56:24,883
Won Ho.

822
00:56:25,023 --> 00:56:26,423
Won Ho, can we talk for a minute?

823
00:56:26,953 --> 00:56:27,953
Won Ho.

824
00:56:28,893 --> 00:56:30,723
- Wait. - Move.

825
00:56:30,863 --> 00:56:31,863
Wait, hold on.

826
00:56:33,793 --> 00:56:34,793
Right now,

827
00:56:34,863 --> 00:56:36,403
our employees and the production crew...

828
00:56:36,403 --> 00:56:39,633
are all waiting for you. If you say you're not doing it now,

829
00:56:39,703 --> 00:56:41,233
what about all the production costs?

830
00:56:41,303 --> 00:56:44,603
Then what about me? I'm so furious that you tricked me...

831
00:56:44,673 --> 00:56:46,573
that I can't do this show or anything else.

832
00:56:46,643 --> 00:56:48,273
What about me? What am I supposed to do?

833
00:56:48,343 --> 00:56:50,383
But I didn't have a choice.

834
00:56:50,813 --> 00:56:52,613
If I hadn't accepted the offer that day,

835
00:56:52,783 --> 00:56:54,813
the appearance would have been cancelled.

836
00:56:54,983 --> 00:56:56,623
What? Would the world end if the appearance was cancelled?

837
00:56:56,683 --> 00:56:57,683
Would we starve to death?

838
00:56:58,223 --> 00:57:00,553
Fine, it was all my fault.

839
00:57:00,623 --> 00:57:01,753
I'm so sorry.

840
00:57:01,823 --> 00:57:03,763
I tricked you and made a fool out of you.

841
00:57:03,823 --> 00:57:07,093
That's all my fault. So please, just this once, okay?

842
00:57:07,433 --> 00:57:08,433
No.

843
00:57:09,363 --> 00:57:11,233
Not for me, for our shop.

844
00:57:11,303 --> 00:57:13,703
Stop using the shop as an excuse. This is all about your greed.

845
00:57:13,833 --> 00:57:16,243
This all happened because you were greedy.

846
00:57:18,403 --> 00:57:19,413
So...

847
00:57:20,813 --> 00:57:22,243
you refuse to do it, no matter what?

848
00:57:22,583 --> 00:57:23,813
Yes. Move.

849
00:57:29,823 --> 00:57:30,823
Wait.

850
00:57:32,123 --> 00:57:33,653
I'm not done talking.

851
00:57:35,363 --> 00:57:36,363
What now?

852
00:57:38,563 --> 00:57:41,063
Fine. I'm...

853
00:57:44,003 --> 00:57:45,003
What was that?

854
00:57:46,673 --> 00:57:47,803
I've made up my mind.

855
00:57:53,143 --> 00:57:54,143
Let's get...

856
00:57:54,973 --> 00:57:56,943
What are you saying? Speak up, I can't hear you.

857
00:58:23,143 --> 00:58:26,043
(Epilogue)

858
00:58:34,113 --> 00:58:36,753
We scraped together every penny we had...

859
00:58:36,823 --> 00:58:38,123
for our new apartment.

860
00:58:38,993 --> 00:58:40,323
And the ceiling is leaking?

861
00:58:40,823 --> 00:58:41,823
Are you serious?

862
00:58:42,023 --> 00:58:43,463
Come on. Still, for people like us,

863
00:58:43,523 --> 00:58:45,763
getting a place this big near the city is a stroke of luck.

864
00:58:46,633 --> 00:58:47,793
Let's look on the bright side.

865
00:58:48,803 --> 00:58:50,803
We can just call someone to fix the ceiling tomorrow.

866
00:58:51,033 --> 00:58:52,903
Still, it's upsetting just looking at it.

867
00:58:53,833 --> 00:58:54,833
It's unsettling.

868
00:58:57,603 --> 00:58:58,773
Then how about we do this?

869
00:59:05,753 --> 00:59:09,583
- How's that? - For a leak, that's not much water.

870
00:59:09,883 --> 00:59:10,883
You think so?

871
00:59:11,253 --> 00:59:12,753
Then should I just bust a hole in the ceiling?

872
00:59:12,823 --> 00:59:14,393
So water comes pouring out like a waterfall?

873
00:59:15,023 --> 00:59:16,193
The house would collapse.

874
00:59:20,333 --> 00:59:21,763
I know things are tough right now,

875
00:59:21,763 --> 00:59:23,203
but please be patient a little longer.

876
00:59:23,933 --> 00:59:25,233
I promise I'll make it big, no matter what.

877
00:59:25,303 --> 00:59:27,573
I'll make sure you get to live in a house like a palace.

878
00:59:28,433 --> 00:59:30,143
So confident.

879
00:59:31,373 --> 00:59:33,213
All right. I believe you.

880
00:59:36,883 --> 00:59:37,943
And what's that...

881
00:59:38,483 --> 00:59:41,083
What's with that other look of confidence?

882
00:59:42,583 --> 00:59:43,683
Since we're bored,

883
00:59:44,523 --> 00:59:45,853
why don't we go to our room for a bit?

884
00:59:46,053 --> 00:59:48,493
Go to our room because we're bored?

885
00:59:48,553 --> 00:59:51,063
What? Let's just go lie down in our room for a bit.

886
00:59:51,123 --> 00:59:53,663
Let's just hang out here. Why do we have to go to our room?

887
00:59:53,733 --> 00:59:55,263
Why? Come on, you're tired.

888
00:59:55,333 --> 00:59:58,803
- What's gotten into you? Suddenly? - No, my knee.

889
00:59:59,273 --> 01:00:00,873
- What's wrong? - Seriously, my knee...

890
01:00:00,933 --> 01:00:01,933
Come here.

891
01:00:02,203 --> 01:00:04,473
Hey, I got you.

892
01:00:18,893 --> 01:00:21,823
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

893
01:00:22,323 --> 01:00:24,963
- Why do you think I threw it? - That was a real Cartier.

894
01:00:25,023 --> 01:00:26,033
So what?

895
01:00:26,093 --> 01:00:27,363
It was a limited edition.

896
01:00:27,433 --> 01:00:28,433
Hey.

897
01:00:29,703 --> 01:00:31,403
I just couldn't believe it.

898
01:00:31,533 --> 01:00:34,333
- Is that really Cheon Man Ju? - She's a Gen Z and millennial icon.

899
01:00:34,403 --> 01:00:36,303
I'm a huge fan of yours.

900
01:00:36,573 --> 01:00:37,743
You throw parties too?

901
01:00:37,803 --> 01:00:38,813
Are you crazy?

902
01:00:38,873 --> 01:00:40,143
You're thinking of going to the Calvin Hotel?

903
01:00:40,213 --> 01:00:42,683
Whatever harm Calvin might do to me now...

904
01:00:42,883 --> 01:00:44,183
is just a drop in the bucket...

905
01:00:44,243 --> 01:00:45,983
compared to how you've torn me apart.

906
01:00:46,053 --> 01:00:47,853
Even if Calvin is divorced,

907
01:00:47,913 --> 01:00:49,583
he wouldn't actually hit on Mi Young, would he?

908
01:00:50,283 --> 01:00:51,683
Why do I have such a bad feeling about this?

909
01:00:51,753 --> 01:00:52,823
Something just feels off.

910
01:00:53,223 --> 01:00:54,223
It's been a while.

